# Source datasets (large downloads; see build/ for how they are fetched)
data/
venv/
build/__pycache__/
build/*.png

# Generated intermediates. docs/ holds the deployable copy of the fields, and
# that is the one GitHub Pages serves -- tracking both meant every field rebuild
# wrote ~300 MB of new blobs into history instead of ~150. The textures here are
# reproducible from build_fields.py / reskin_seafloor.py; the manifest is not
# (five build scripts read it), so it is kept deliberately.
web/fields/
!web/fields/manifest.json
web/frames/
web/artifact.html
web/bluemarble.jpg

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# Finder / iCloud conflict copies: "fut_0005_e 2.webp" beside "fut_0005_e.webp".
# The project lives under Desktop, so these keep reappearing in docs/fields
# after build_site.py wipes and rebuilds it. They are byte-identical to the
# originals and pure deploy bloat, but `git add -A docs` would happily commit
# 600+ of them and roughly double what GitHub Pages has to serve.
* [0-9].webp
* [0-9].json
* [0-9].html

# Intermediate age/isochron grids -- rebuildable, ~400 MB, never shipped
build/cache/
data/Muller2019_PresentDay_AgeGrid.nc

# Reference material for the sea-floor work: ~80 large screenshots and
# process diagrams, several hundred MB. README §11 describes what is in it.
Deep Time Maps and Resources/
build/verify/
